# Routes the @ipaas scope (adapter-connectwise, adapter-keka) to GitHub
# Packages instead of the public npm registry -- that's the only place
# these packages are published (see ipaas.providers/*/package.json's
# publishConfig, and .github/workflows/publish-providers.yml at the repo
# root). Everything else still resolves from the public registry as usual.
#
# GitHub Packages requires auth even to install/read a package, not just to
# publish one. ${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN} is resolved from the environment at
# install time -- npm supports this substitution natively, this file never
# contains a real token:
#   - Local dev: set NODE_AUTH_TOKEN once in your own shell profile to a
#     GitHub PAT with read:packages scope -- see docs/setup/DEVELOPER_SETUP.md.
#   - CI / Docker build: NODE_AUTH_TOKEN is set for the duration of a single
#     `npm ci` step from a build secret, never baked into an image layer or
#     committed anywhere -- see Dockerfile and
#     .github/workflows/build-orchestration-engine.yml.
#
# This file is unrelated to `npm link` -- link overrides whatever's in
# node_modules with a symlink to the local ipaas.providers checkout,
# regardless of where node_modules originally came from. This .npmrc only
# controls what a real `npm install`/`npm ci` (no link involved) resolves
# @ipaas/* to.
@ipaas:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN}
